Package: AdaptiveBoxplot
Title: Unified Boxplots for Outlier Detection via Multiple Testing. The package include functions 
    for producing FDR(BH) boxplot and FWER(Holm) boxplot
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bowen", "Gang", email = "bgang@fudan.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Hongmei", "Lin", email = "hmlin@suibe.edu.cn", role = "aut"),
    person("Tiejun", "Tong", email = "tongt@hkbu.edu.hk", role = "aut"))
Description: Implements a novel framework for creating boxplots where the 
    whisker lengths are determined by formal multiple testing procedures, 
    making them adaptive to sample size and data characteristics. This package 
    provides functions to generate boxplots that control the False Discovery 
    Rate (FDR) via the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure and the Family-Wise 
    Error Rate (FWER) via the Holm procedure. These methods provide a 
    statistically principled and powerful alternative to the classic Tukey boxplot for outlier detection.
    The methods are based on the framework by Gang, Lin, and Tong (2025). 
